# __CRATE__-admin / CRATE_API

## Role

Owner-specific operator workspace with a server-paginated record table, a
localized editor and a dual-path record API.

## Platform Capability Bindings

The native path extracts trusted platform request context and binds the owner
to the host's settings reader. The CSR path uses the platform GraphQL client.
The settings view requires module management authority. Its exact native
and GraphQL reads share the host's operator reader. Settings writes use the
platform GraphQL mutation and preserve settings outside the edited section.
The grid and UI catalog use the effective locale supplied by the Leptos host.

## Domain Collaborations

The record owner alone decides authorization, localization fallback, state
transitions, revisions and durable effects.

## Minimum Contract Set

### Input DTOs/Commands

The transport facade lists, reads, creates drafts, edits a title in an
explicit locale, and sets publication state. Edits carry the applied revision
as a decimal string.

The editor opens an explicit language before editing its title. Save sends
the revision and language loaded from the owner. Publication actions use
the same revision contract and require the current title to be saved or
discarded first.

A settings submission carries the owner-issued settings revision and a
client-generated idempotency key. After a conflict or an unconfirmed save,
the form retains the draft and asks the operator to reload the saved values.

### Domain Invariants

Authenticated authority belongs to one active tenant. Read fallback does not
choose a write locale. Clients get the requested, effective and available
locales with each returned record.

### Events / Outbox Side Effects

Publication and edits to published titles trigger the owner's durable Search
projection events.

### Errors / Failure Codes

The facade exposes known owner refusals and keeps transport failures as
separate evidence for the selected path. Native endpoint errors mask internal
database, settings and event details. Unconfirmed writes are never replayed
automatically.
